==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|Ri-verbs}}
{{wikipedia|Ri-sögn|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|gnúa}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*ganū(w)aną}}, cognate with {{cog|got|𐌱𐌽𐌰𐌿𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈnuːa/}}
* {{rhymes|is|uːa|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-ri|neri|11=néri|núið}}

# to [[rub]], to [[chafe]]

====Usage notes====
* One of the four [[w:is:Ri-sagnir|ri-verbs]] in Icelandic, the other being {{m|is|snúa||to turn}}, {{m|is|gróa||to grow; to heal}} and {{m|is|róa||to row}}.
* As with the other ri-verbs, the past tense {{m|is||neri}} was originally pronounced with an ''e'' sound but is today pronounced with a ''[[é]]'' sound. There are therefore two spelling variants used: {{m|is||neri}} and {{m|is||néri}}. The Icelandic Ministry of Education considers both variants to be equally correct,<ref>[https://ritreglur.arnastofnun.is/ Icelandic Ministry of Education - Announcements regarding orthography from 2016 and 2018, section 3.5.5]</ref> but many speakers consider the original {{m|is||neri}} spelling to be the more correct one.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to rub}} {{l|is|nudda}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|núa um nasir}}
* {{l|is|núa saman höndum}}

